        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.14,
          "end": 3.91,
          "en": "Now, setup does not just get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.91,
          "end": 5.69,
          "en": "this props parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.69,
          "end": 7.76,
          "en": "It also gets a second parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.76,
          "end": 11.28,
          "en": "A second argument is always fed in by vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.28,
          "end": 14.2,
          "en": "and that's the context object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.2,
          "end": 15.807,
          "en": "We can console.log(context) here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.75,
          "end": 18.2,
          "en": "to see what's inside of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.74,
          "end": 22.04,
          "en": "If I saved that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.04,
          "end": 23.53,
          "en": "it looks like an empty object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.53,
          "end": 24.75,
          "en": "but actually if we inspect it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.75,
          "end": 27.6,
          "en": "we see three important properties in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 30.463,
          "en": "Attrs, emit and slots.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.59,
          "end": 35.76,
          "en": "attrs are any fall through attributes you might have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.76,
          "end": 39.58,
          "en": "So if you set something like let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.58,
          "end": 43.03,
          "en": "a class here on user data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.03,
          "end": 46.14,
          "en": "and class is not a prop you define here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.14,
          "end": 49.3,
          "en": "then it's automatically a fall through prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.3,
          "end": 51.63,
          "en": "It's an optional prop you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.63,
          "end": 54.09,
          "en": "Here in this case, actually, if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.09,
          "end": 57.24,
          "en": "I will get a warning because there's fall through behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.24,
          "end": 60.5,
          "en": "doesn't really work if you have multiple route nodes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.5,
          "end": 65.373,
          "en": "But if I wrap this in one route node here, like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.24,
          "end": 69.68,
          "en": "and then reload, the warning is gone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.68,
          "end": 73.23,
          "en": "and now under attrs, if we inspect the Target,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.23,
          "end": 76.67,
          "en": "we see our class here with the test value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.67,
          "end": 79.07,
          "en": "So that's attrs it's properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.07,
          "end": 81.12,
          "en": "which you didn't define as properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.12,
          "end": 82.883,
          "en": "which just fall through.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.94,
          "end": 87.46000000000001,
          "en": "slots would give you access to any slot data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.46000000000001,
          "end": 89.42,
          "en": "you might have in your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.42,
          "end": 91.69,
          "en": "This of course is a component without slots",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.69,
          "end": 93.65,
          "en": "but if you had a slot in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.65,
          "end": 96.43,
          "en": "you could access the slots data programmatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.43,
          "end": 99.203,
          "en": "through that slot property on context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.27000000000001,
          "end": 101.99000000000001,
          "en": "And emit is a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.99000000000001,
          "end": 104.68,
          "en": "which you can call to emit a custom event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.68,
          "end": 107.09,
          "en": "because of course, that's also something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.09,
          "end": 108.72,
          "en": "you often need to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 108.72,
          "end": 111.46000000000001,
          "en": "And with the options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.46000000000001,
          "end": 114.57,
          "en": "we always use this dollar sign $emit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.57,
          "end": 116.22999999999999,
          "en": "Now, since this keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.22999999999999,
          "end": 118.63,
          "en": "as you learned isn't available here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.63,
          "end": 122.61,
          "en": "This dollar sign emit is not available in the setup method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.61,
          "end": 126.58,
          "en": "Still of course you might have code that needs to emit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.58,
          "end": 129.49,
          "en": "In that case, you have context emit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.49,
          "end": 133.27,
          "en": "and that works just like this emit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.27,
          "end": 137.11,
          "en": "So if you had a safe data custom event, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.11,
          "end": 139.31,
          "en": "with some data you wanna emit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.31,
          "end": 143.97,
          "en": "the equivalent to this options API syntax would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.97,
          "end": 147.553,
          "en": "this syntax here with context emit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.67000000000002,
          "end": 149.86,
          "en": "We don't need it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.86,
          "end": 151.763,
          "en": "but it is worth being aware of that.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
